---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Algorithmic Art Gallery by Jonathan R. Reed"
  description="Privacy notes for Algorithmic Art Gallery, including local generator settings, saved artwork behavior, exports, and public site interactions."
>
  <section class="info-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy notes for a browser-based art tool.</h1>
    <p class="mono-text info-byline">
      By Jonathan R. Reed. Updated <time datetime="2026-04-21">April 21, 2026</time>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Algorithmic Art Gallery is designed as a public creative tool. Generator
      settings such as seed, curve, growth mode, symmetry, and export choices
      are used to render artwork in the browser. The project does not require a
      visitor account, login, payment details, or private profile to create an
      image.
    </p>
    <p>
      Treat generated artwork like any file you choose to download or share.
      Exports may contain visible details from the composition and any naming
      choices you apply outside the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      The generator is meant to work without a user account. Most creative state
      belongs to the browser session, the local device, or files you decide to
      export. If you share a generated image elsewhere, that platform may apply
      its own metadata, storage, and privacy practices.
    </p>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <article>
        <h2>Artwork settings</h2>
        <p>
          Saved pieces and exported files are part of the user-facing creative
          workflow. Avoid entering confidential project names or private client
          details into artwork labels, filenames, or gallery notes unless you
          are comfortable storing or sharing them.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Site operation</h2>
        <p>
          Normal hosting requests and browser behavior may be used to serve the
          site, load assets, and support basic operation. External portfolio and
          project links lead to separate sites with their own privacy practices.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          If the browser saves preferences or gallery state, those values are
          meant to support the local creative workflow. Clear site data in your
          browser if you want to reset saved settings.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p>
      Do not enter private client names, confidential project titles, or sensitive
      identifiers into artwork labels or filenames unless you are comfortable
      keeping those details on your device or in exported files.
    </p>
    <p class="info-actions">
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      <a href="/gallery/">Gallery</a>
      <a href="/">Generator</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
